1. Relation to PySAL
--------------------
Spatex reimplements, in Rust and Elixir, functionality of the PySAL ecosystem
(https://pysal.org): libpysal, esda, mapclassify, pointpats, spreg, mgwr,
spglm, giddy, inequality and spopt. The implementations were written against
those packages: they follow the published methods, the packages'
documentation and their source code, so that results, defaults and documented
quirks agree, and they are checked against output produced by the packages
themselves (section 4). docs/parity.md maps every function and lists each
known deviation.

The files listed in section 2 translate specific upstream functions. The rest
of the Rust and Elixir code is written for Spatex: it is not a line-by-line
translation, although some modules follow the upstream code's decomposition
function by function (for example the Max-p, AZP and random-region heuristics
follow spopt's) while using their own data structures and random streams.


